      "prompt": "A series RC circuit (resistor R, capacitor C, battery 𝓔, switch) is analyzed at three moments: right after the switch closes, at t=RC (one time constant later), and a very long time later. (a) Compare the current at t=0 to the current a long time later, justifying. (b) At t=RC, is the capacitor's voltage closer to 0, to 𝓔, or at roughly 63% of the way to 𝓔? Explain what one time constant physically represents. (c) If R is increased (C, 𝓔 unchanged), does the circuit take longer or shorter to approach full charge? Explain.",
